Section 25.
The Board shall have powers and duties as follows:
to propose to the Council of Ministers measures for money
laundering control;to consider and give opinions to the Minister with regard to the
issuing of Ministerial Regulations, rules and notifications
for the execution of this Act;
to lay down rules in connection with the retention, a sale
by auctionor utilisation of property and the evaluation of compensation and depreciation under
section 57;
to promote public co-operation in connection with the giving of
information for the purpose of money laundering control;
to monitor and evaluate the execution of this Act;
to perform other acts prescribed in this Act or other laws.

